 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\nYou can use the transaction ETOUEXCEPTO1 (accessed from the SAP Easy Access Menu as follows: |\u00bbUtilities Industry > Billing\nTime-of-Use Exceptions Monitor and Edit Time-of-Use Exceptions %) to monitor and edit time-of-use exceptions. You can also\nuse it to create, change, and delete TOU exceptions or their activation status. You can also navigate to the relevant TOU exception\n\nprogram and the relevant TOU exception responses.\n\nPrerequisites\n\nTo be able to create TOU exceptions, an appropriate TOU exception program is required. You create TOU exception programs in\n\nCustomizing for SAP Utilities: |}/Advanced Metering Infrastructure \u00bb Time-of-Use Interface \u00bb Define Time-of-Use Exception\nProgram\n\nFeatures\n\nYou can select the TOU exceptions you want to monitor or edit using a combination of different criteria, such as a user name, a\nspecific period of time, an exception program ID, or an exception text. You can also restrict the number of TOU exceptions selected\nby making an entry in the Restrict Number To field. For more information about the possible selection criteria and the\ncombinations available, see the documentation for the report REEXCEPTION DISP_MAINT.\n\nMonitoring of TOU Exceptions\n\nYou can use the Change Layout function to add additional fields (such as administration data and texts). By selecting a line and\nchoosing |}Goto \u00bb Exception Response 3, you can navigate to the available TOU exception responses for the selected TOU\nexception. Here, you can change or delete the responses, or you can change the activation status - see Monitor and Process Time-\nof-Use Exception Responses.\n\nCreating TOU Exceptions\n\nThe From/To time information is in the same time zone as the selected TOU exception program. You can determine the predefined\n\ntime period in the BAd| ISU_TOUEXCEPT_ TIME, method SET FROM TO DATE_TIME. If the activation category of the TOU\nexception program is not Active for Individual Customers, the TOU exceptions may not overlap. In addition, a TOU exception must\n\nbe in the time period of the TOU exception program. The From/To time information must match the interval length of the\nappropriate TOU interface.\n\n1 Note\n\nIf the TOU exception program is not linked to a conditional billing program in Customizing, the check does not take place. Also\nnote that the system does not check whether the TOU exception period is part of a period that has already been billed for a\nrelevant installation.\n\nWhen a TOU exception is created, the activation status is set to Active. You can determine the default status in the BAdI\n\nISU TOUEXCEPT STATUS, method SET ACTIVATION STATUS When you create a TOU exception, the activation status (Active\nor Inactive) is set automatically.\n\nChange TOU Exception\n\nWhen you change a TOU exception, the system carries out the same checks that are carried out duing creation. You can only\nchange a TOU exception if it has not yet been billed. You can view all changes to TOU exceptions by selecting a line and choosing\nGoto Change Document *\u00a5. Note that the From/To time information is in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). Also, the Text for\nTOU Exception Program field is not entered in the change document.\n",
